# v2.3.5717 (card SEC PR 18): THE SITE'S PROTECTIVE HEADERS, ON EVERY PAGE.
# They lived in src/public/_headers, which the build never copied (vite.config.js:
# root 'src', publicDir '../public'), so production sent none of them.  Here,
# where Pages reads them (dist/_headers):
#   - X-Frame-Options and Content-Security-Policy frame-ancestors: no other site
#     may show the game inside its own page (a page that frames the game can lay
#     its own buttons over ours).  The repository and its docs name no place the
#     game is shown inside another site's page.  To allow ONE named site later,
#     replace both lines' values with that site, e.g.
#       Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://example.com
#     and delete the X-Frame-Options line (it cannot name a site).
#   - X-Content-Type-Options: a file is read as the type it is sent as.
#   - Referrer-Policy: another site is told only our address, never the page.
# A header has no live switch: a change here is a new build.  A pull request's
# preview URL serves this file too, so a change shows there first.
# tools/guards/site-headers.test.mjs fails if src/public/_headers comes back.
#
# v2.3.5820 (card SEC2, the owner's outside audit of 2026-11-17): three more.
#   - Strict-Transport-Security: a browser that has been here once goes
#     straight to https:// for a year, so a coffee-shop network cannot catch
#     the first plain-http request and answer it itself.  includeSubDomains
#     holds api.brotown.net (the worker) the same way; every name under
#     brotown.net is served by Cloudflare over https.  NOT `preload`: that
#     asks the browsers to build the rule in for good, months to undo, and is
#     the owner's call (hstspreload.org) once this has run a while.
#   - Permissions-Policy: the camera, microphone, location, payments, USB and
#     motion sensors are switched off for the page and anything it frames.
#     The game uses none of them (census 2026-11-17).  NOT switched off,
#     because the game uses them: fullscreen and the orientation lock
#     (BroTown.jsx), the clipboard, the share sheet, vibrate, autoplay.
#   - Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: the list of places the page may
#     load from, REPORT-ONLY: a browser that sees something off the list
#     still loads it and writes a warning in the console.  The audit's own
#     advice: never switch a full policy on blind, a wrong line is a black
#     screen.  Each source, and why (census 2026-11-17):
#       script  'self'; Turnstile (challenges.cloudflare.com, verify.js);
#               the hash is index.html's one inline handler, the font
#               preload's onload (it moves the sheet in without blocking);
#               'unsafe-eval' because PixiJS 8 builds its shader code with
#               new Function and REFUSES TO START without it (AbstractRenderer:
#               "does not allow unsafe-eval"): the audit's own script-src
#               'self' is a black screen.  Dropping it means importing
#               pixi.js/unsafe-eval first, a renderer change of its own;
#       style   'self', inline (index.html's loading screen, React), the
#               Google Fonts sheet;  font: fonts.gstatic.com;
#       img     'self', data: (game.css), blob: (bakes, keepAsImage) and any
#               https: (a bro's NFT picture, through wsrv.nl or its host);
#       media   'self', data: (GameApp's silent wav), blob:;
#       connect 'self', the worker (https and wss api.brotown.net), the NFT
#               catalogue (raw.githubusercontent.com), Turnstile;
#       worker  'self' (png8Worker, bodyBakeWorker, the ground worker);
#       frame   Turnstile's box;  object none;  base and form 'self'.
#     frame-ancestors stays in the enforced line above (a report-only policy
#     cannot carry it).  To switch it on: test it on a preview URL (the
#     console shows "[Report Only]" warnings, none expected), then rename
#     the header to Content-Security-Policy and fold the frame-ancestors line
#     in.  docs/plan/cards/SEC2.md has the steps.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=(), accelerometer=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-hashes' 'sha256-1jAmyYXcRq6zFldLe/GCgIDJBiOONdXjTLgEFMDnDSM=' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://api.brotown.net wss://api.brotown.net https://raw.githubusercontent.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# v2.3.2330: cache headers for Cloudflare Pages.  Vite copies public/ into
# dist/ verbatim, which is where Pages reads this from; there was no _headers
# file anywhere before, so every one of the ~700 assets on a repeat load was
# revalidated -- bytes saved, round trips not.
#
# ONLY the content-hashed tree.  /assets/* filenames carry a build hash, so a
# changed file is a new URL and "immutable" can never serve a stale one.  The
# sprite and audio trees are NOT here: many of their URLs are cache-busted by a
# ?v= that the code appends, but not all of them are, and a year of immutable
# on a file that quietly changes is the "it looks fine for me" bug.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.2959: the Wheel's ground pictures (public/world/ground/).  The owner's
# phone fell behind walking the Wheel on a slow connection: every tile was
# revalidated, a round trip each, every visit.  The worker asks for each at
# ?v=<its manifest's date>, so a new upload is a new address and keeping the
# old one forever is safe; the manifest itself is fetched at a fresh address
# every time (public/tools/world/core/ground-worker.js).
/world/ground/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.3298: the Wheel's baked objects and map pictures (public/world/placed/,
# tools/world/bake-wheel-world.mjs).  The ground worker asks for each at
# ?v=<the bake's fingerprint> (public/tools/world/core/placed.js), so a new
# bake is a new address and keeping the old one for a year is safe.
/world/placed/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.3319: and the long Wheel's (public/world/placed5/, v2.3.3315) -- this
# rule was missing, so its 700 KB of objects and pictures were asked about
# again on every visit -- with the world map's detail tiles in placed5/detail/
# (src/ui/worldMapDetail.js), at the same ?v=.
/world/placed5/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.3258: the pictures of the inside of each building (public/world/
# interiors/, ~300 KB each).  Asked for at ?v=<ROOMS_V> (src/data/
# buildingRooms.js), so replacing one is a new address and a year of immutable
# is safe; the game fetches the other rooms' bytes in idle moments after the
# first door (src/game/buildingRooms.js), and a second visit costs nothing.
/world/interiors/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.3566: the dungeons' pictures (public/world/dungeons/), the owner's: each
# entrance, its walls and the things in its arena, and the boss's chest.  The
# game asks for each at ?v=<DUNGEON_ART_V> (src/data/dungeonArt.js, written by
# tools/world/add-dungeon-art.mjs with every run), so a new cut is a new address.
/world/dungeons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.3136: the farm's pictures (public/world/farm/), the owner's.  The game
# asks for each at ?v=<FARM_ART_V> (src/data/farmArt.js, written by
# tools/world/add-farm-art.mjs with every run), so a new cut is a new address.
# Nothing in the game fetches manifest.json; whatever does must ask at a fresh
# address, as the ground's worker does.
/world/farm/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.6742: the sounds (public/sfx/), card KEEP PR 3.  Every request the game
# makes here carries its file's version (?v=, the first 10 characters of the
# SHA-256 of its bytes: tools/assets/versions.mjs): the build writes it into
# every written-out address, and src/game/assetUrl.js into a built one.  So a
# changed sound is a new address and a year of immutable is safe.  Held by
# tools/guards/keep-sfx.test.mjs (a bare or built address that skips the
# version, and the census's count for this folder, which must be 0).
/sfx/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# v2.3.6744: the world's object sheets (public/world/objects/), card KEEP PR
# 3c.  Every request the game makes here carries its file's version (?v=, the
# first 10 characters of the SHA-256 of its bytes): each sheet and its page
# through src/game/assetUrl.js (src/rendering/wheelObjects.js, the farm's copy
# in farmWorld.js at `&farm=1`), the page at its OWN version, never the
# sheet's copied on (sheetPage.js, png8Worker.js); the manifest at the version
# the page posts the ground worker.  So a changed sheet is a new address and a
# year of immutable is safe.  Held by tools/guards/keep-sfx.test.mjs.
/world/objects/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
